WEEK4:
OM - Object model 
like tree with node attributes & leafs 

HTML → DOM (from HTML file we build the tree with like body head etc)
every element becomes a node {even <style> but not the rules inside it }
<link> or <img> start same time as DOM is being created when found in the HTML file

CSS → CSSOM (from CSS we build tree with all color size font width etc)
tree of CSS rules 
cascading -> rules go down from parent to child

JavaScript → can change DOM or CSSOM (using code we can change ant rule and perform functions on it)


FLOW:
1 . DOM+CSSOM -combine these 2 together and get RENDER TREE
  Render tree -> contains only visible nodes so if anything has [ display: none ] will be only present in DOM/CSSOM
2. run LAYOUT on render tree -> to get the overall geomentry 
3. PAINT the pixels on the screen as a website for user 

DEVTOOLS

DOMCONENTLOADED - At whatever time the DOM tree finishes building 
LOAD - at whatever time the whole page loads including the CSS JS imgs links 

Flow:
Browser first downloads HTML.
While parsing HTML, it sees image tag.
Image download starts during parsing.
DOMContentLoaded can happen before image finishes. {Browser can reserve <img> space and paint page before image fully downloads}<- so does not block rendering
load waits until image finishes.

now what if external JS and CSS present as link? 
- CSS can block rendering because browser needs CSSOM for render tree.
- JS can block parsing unless async/defer is used.
- Downloads may happen in parallel, but they start at different times depending on when parser discovers them. <- can view this in network waterfall 
After load browser can still ask for extre resources -> cause they dont affect the page as much and dont matter in the tree


MEASURING PERFORMANCE :

CRITICAL RESOURCE:
HTML = 5KB
CSS = 4KB
JS = 10KB   -> these 3 essential for rendering
NOTE: An image is usually not critical because browser can calculate its layout space and paint before the image finishes loading.

CRITICAL PATH LENGTH:
Number of round trips needed to fetch all critical resources.
Example: HTML downloads -> JS, then JS downloads -> another JS.

Critical path length = 3 round trips.
If resources download in parallel, only the longest dependency chain counts.

CRITICAL SIZE:
Total size of critical resources needed before rendering.
Critical bytes = 19KB from 1st example.

